<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Yeh Bro is gym education from an experienced lifter’s point of view — training, food, recovery, and honest talk about bodybuilding culture when you’re ready for it."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<article class="prose-wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>Experienced gym guidance. Straight talk.</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Yeh Bro is how I’d walk someone toward the best shape of their life — training that compounds,
			food that isn’t obsessive, sleep that recovers you, and honest literacy about gym culture when
			you go deeper. Start with the path, not the rabbit holes.
		</p>

		<h2>Who this is for</h2>
		<p>
			People who train (or are about to) and want clear structure: what to do this week, what to ignore,
			and how to think about cuts, bulks, and bloodwork without forum cosplay. If you want a numbered
			on-ramp, use <a href="/start-here">Start here</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>How I think about progress</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Process over peak stills</strong> — sessions completed, lifts trending, weight moving the direction you chose</li>
			<li><strong>Simple programs longer</strong> — progressive overload on patterns you can repeat</li>
			<li><strong>Protein and sleep before exotic tubs</strong> — creatine earns a place; most stacks don’t</li>
			<li><strong>Phases when ready</strong> — cut → settle → lean surplus; see the <a href="/blog/bodybuilding-blueprint">bodybuilding blueprint</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Culture literacy (later, not first)</h2>
		<p>
			Bodybuilding has a pharmacology shadow. Pretending it doesn’t exist helps nobody. Leading beginners
			with it helps fewer. When you’re ready, we teach risks, bloodwork as clinical care, legality at a
			high level, and coming off under a clinician — as <strong>education</strong>, not a protocol from
			this site and not a storefront.
		</p>
		<p>
			Start with
			<a href="/blog/bodybuilding-culture-education">bodybuilding culture</a> and
			<a href="/blog/ped-harm-reduction-australia">PED harm reduction</a> after the Start-here basics.
			Bloodwork pathways some readers research (not affiliated): 
			<a href="https://roidsafe.com.au" rel="noopener noreferrer">RoidSafe</a>,
			<a href="https://pedtestaustralia.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">PED Test Australia</a>. Prefer a
			clinician who knows your history.
		</p>

		<h2>Products we mention</h2>
		<p>
			When a guide links a tub, it’s legal sports nutrition that fits an evidence-first stack —
			creatine, protein, pre/basics — judged on labels, dose clarity, and value. Quiet
			<code>/go/</code> links may earn a commission; full detail on
			<a href="/disclosure">Disclosure</a>. We don’t source AAS, SARMs, peptides, or underground gear.
		</p>

		<div class="cta-row">
